\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The Field Origin as a vortex core. \textbf  {Left:} A river whirlpool viewed from the side. Water spirals inward at the surface, passes through the vortex core, and disperses below. \textbf  {Right:} The three structural states of the dual tetrad. TetA spacetime (purple, top) in the forward-orientation state, the Field Origin (red, center) at the coupling boundary where $\tau _{\text  {prop}} = 0$, and TetB spacetime (blue, bottom) in the reversed-orientation state. Double-headed arrows indicate that the field propagates through each sector; the labels (Forward, Reversed) describe the tetrad orientation, a structural property of the coupling hierarchy.}}{23}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
